There are several ways you can implement this method.  This is one way to do it.



Start with input validation:

Check if the kiloBytes parameter is less than 0. If it is, print "Invalid Value" to the console and use the return statement to exit the method.

Calculate the megabytes and remaining kilobytes:

To convert kilobytes to megabytes, divide the kiloBytes parameter by 1024. Store the result in an int variable, say mb.

To find the remaining kilobytes, use the modulo operator (%). Calculate kiloBytes % 1024 and store the result in an int variable, say remainingKB.

Print the result:

Use System.out.println to print the conversion result to the console in the format: kiloBytes + " KB = " + mb + " MB and " + remainingKB + " KB".